# Verification

- Inspect the existing test setup and project scripts before choosing commands.
- For behavior changes, add or update tests for the expected behavior and relevant failure cases.
- Prefer deterministic tests; mock external Gemini API calls in ordinary unit tests.
- Run the narrowest relevant tests first, then broader checks when appropriate.
- Run applicable lint, type-check, test, and build commands.
- Never weaken assertions, remove tests, or silently skip checks just to obtain a green result.
- Report exact commands run and their outcomes.
- If a check cannot run, explain why.
  